chapter13(seq(65,84),'Manual review required','Table footnotes require reference/footnote identification, order across columns, placement, numbering restart, note/source sequencing, layout and typography. General source offsets and page numbers do not certify footnote structure. Known conflicts with LCB sentence-opening numeral forms must be excluded if automated later.');
chapter13([85,86],'Manual review required','Fraction alignment and figure versus word form depend on table cell versus footnote roles and source typography. General bill fraction checks deliberately exclude tables; this does not establish these table rules.');
chapter13([87,88],'Manual review required','Headnotes require identifying table notes separately from body text and enforcing type/size, bracket/punctuation and continuation treatment. A plain-text line or bracket alone is insufficient.');
