chapter7([1,2,3,4,5],'Manual review required','These instructions define the example list’s deliberately incomplete scope and GPO compounding authority, distinct from its spelling dictionary. Selected compounds do not cover every omitted -ed modifier, open form or productive prefix/suffix analogy. Full-list search is available; dictionary preference alone is not safe compounding evidence.');
chapter7([6,8,11],'Manual review required','Literal versus nonliteral meaning, accidental adjacent words and differently pronounced lookalike words require actual sentence meaning. Unrestricted joining would corrupt phrases such as side line or some one. Selected explicit noun/verb checks do not establish all these distinctions.');
chapter7([7],'Partially automated','Selected LCB/GPO-compatible unit modifiers and narrowly identified predicate adjectives are checked separately. Explicit crystal-clear water/fire-tested material examples distinguish the two positions and retain their source noun restriction when linked to complete known compounds, selected ordinary adjectives or already-open source predicates by a final conjunction. Selected finite-clause and terminal reduced/statutory boundaries distinguish supported comma continuations from embedded noun phrases. This does not establish arbitrary noun heads, unlisted adjective coordination, predicative scope or every analogue; full sentence meaning and source quotations remain manual.');
chapter7([9],'Partially automated','Selected solid and hyphenated prefixes are checked with listed examples and LCB-compatible exceptions. Vowel doubling, capitalization, pronunciation and prefixes attached to compounds require contextual interpretation; unknown productive forms are not universally joined.');
chapter7([10],'Partially automated','461 explicit particle-ending noun entries from the column-preserved GPO table have open-variant checks after a determiner and before a recognized nominal continuation. These include holdup/calldown/layout/makeup and run-in/run-on/tie-in. Selected LCB-listed solid compounds after modal verbs are checked as separate-word verbs. Other grammatical contexts, plurals, -er derivatives and the remaining compounding table stay manual; source lookup is not full automation.');
chapter7([12,13],'Manual review required','The flush keyword, indentation, space-mark and part-of-speech abbreviations govern interpretation of this multi-column lexical table. Whole-table hierarchy and every entry’s noun/verb/modifier/prefix exception are not fully mapped to tested checks; page search must not be counted as automation.');
